<title>JAPAN: Tokyo June consumer prices up 1.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Tokyo June consumer prices up 1.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo area consumer prices rose 1.9 percent in June from a year earlier, while nationwide consumer prices for May also rose 1.9 percent year-on-year, the government's Management and Coordination Agency said on Friday.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of consumer prices in Tokyo and nationwide (index base 1995):</p>
<p>				     JUNE	MAY	 APR</p>
<p> Tokyo overall index	   101.9     101.8     101.5</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes		+1.9pct   +1.4pct   +1.2pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	    +0.1pct   +0.3pct   +1.7pct</p>
<p> Tokyo core index		101.8     101.8     101.5</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes		+1.7pct   +1.6pct   +1.4pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	     0.0pct   +0.3pct   +1.5pct</p>
<p>				     MAY	 APR	 MAR</p>
<p> Nationwide overall index    102.4     102.2     100.2</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes		+1.9pct   +1.9pct   +0.5pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	    +0.2pct   +2.0pct   +0.1pct</p>
<p> Nationwide core index	 102.4     102.2     100.3</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes		+2.1pct   +2.0pct   +0.5pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	    +0.2pct   +1.9pct   +0.3pct</p>
<p>(Note: The Tokyo index is calculated by collecting price data at mid-month. The core index, which is a key barometer for gauging core inflation, is overall prices minus fresh food prices. The base year has been changed to 1995 from 1990.)</p>
</text>
